1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:01,700
In 1920,

2
00:00:01,700 --> 00:00:02,600
one man promised

3
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:03,500
to grow your money

4
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:04,660
by 50%

5
00:00:04,660 --> 00:00:06,530
in 45 days.

6
00:00:06,550 --> 00:00:07,730
Charles Ponzi said

7
00:00:07,730 --> 00:00:08,490
he was trading

8
00:00:08,490 --> 00:00:11,021
international postal coupons.

9
00:00:11,041 --> 00:00:12,427
He wasn't.

10
00:00:12,447 --> 00:00:13,707
He paid early investors

11
00:00:13,707 --> 00:00:14,667
with money from

12
00:00:14,667 --> 00:00:15,547
new ones,

13
00:00:15,547 --> 00:00:15,927
and the crowds

14
00:00:15,927 --> 00:00:17,266
kept coming.

15
00:00:17,286 --> 00:00:18,746
When reporters checked,

16
00:00:18,746 --> 00:00:19,506
there weren't enough coupons

17
00:00:19,506 --> 00:00:20,386
in the world

18
00:00:20,386 --> 00:00:21,345
to cover it.

19
00:00:21,365 --> 00:00:22,085
The scheme collapsed

20
00:00:22,085 --> 00:00:22,725
in August,

21
00:00:22,725 --> 00:00:23,945
and it still carries

22
00:00:23,945 --> 00:00:24,881
his name.
